Maven Build Workflow: The Maven lifecycle is a structured sequence of build phases that automate the build and deployment process for projects.
📌 Phases within the Default Lifecycle: 
✅ Validate: Verifies the project's structure and information.
✅ Compile: Compiles the project's source code.
✅ Test: Executes unit tests.
✅ Package: Packages the compiled code into a distributable format (e.g., JAR, WAR).
✅ Verify: Checks the package for quality issues.
✅ Install: Installs the package into the local Maven repository.
✅ Deploy: Deploys the package to a remote repository. 
